<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine unions plan reaction to labor reforms.</title>
<headline>Argentine unions plan reaction to labor reforms.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The leadership of Argentina's main CGT union federation met Friday to discuss how to react to President Carlos Menem's decision to sign three decrees on labor market reforms.</p>
<p>CGT leaders started their meeting at 1830 local time (2130 GMT) to ponder how to react to the decrees.</p>
<p>Late Wednesday Menem decided to end weeks of negotiations with the unions and bypass reluctant lawmakers by introducing the first labor reforms by decree.</p>
<p>Unions staged a 36-hour general strike in September in opposition to the labor market reforms and other government measures.</p>
<p>((-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0668))</p>
</text>
